<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d6" for="edge" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d5" for="edge" attr.name="keywords" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d4" for="edge" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d3" for="edge" attr.name="weight" attr.type="double" />
  <key id="d2" for="node" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="node" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;CIVIDALE DEL FRIULI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cividale del Friuli is a town and 'comune' in the Province of Udine, part of the Friuli-Venezia Giulia region of northern Italy, situated above sea level in the foothills of the eastern Alps, near the Slovenian border, and known for its medieval center and archaeological findings."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0192-b3372c1e155b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UDINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Udine is a city in the Province of Udine, Italy, from which Cividale del Friuli is accessible by rail."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0192-b3372c1e155b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FRIULI-VENEZIA GIULIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Friuli-Venezia Giulia is a region in northern Italy where Cividale del Friuli is located."&lt;SEP&gt;"Friuli-Venezia Giulia is a region in northern Italy where the cuisine is unique and appreciated by the author."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0192-b3372c1e155b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EASTERN ALPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Eastern Alps are a mountain range where Cividale del Friuli is situated in the foothills."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0192-b3372c1e155b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NATISONE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Natisone is a river that flows through Cividale del Friuli, forming a picturesque ravine."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0192-b3372c1e155b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VENETI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Veneti were an ancient people who first settled the area around Cividale del Friuli."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0192-b3372c1e155b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CELTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Celts were another ancient group that initially inhabited the region around Cividale del Friuli."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0192-b3372c1e155b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ITALY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Italy is the country where Cividale del Friuli is located."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0192-b3372c1e155b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FRIULI-VENEZIA GIULIA TOURIST &amp; TRAVEL INFORMATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Friuli-Venezia Giulia Tourist &amp; Travel Information provides tourist and travel information about the region."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0192-b3372c1e155b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CIVIDALE DEL FRIULI : TOURIST AND TRAVEL GUIDE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cividale del Friuli : Tourist and Travel Guide is a guide providing information about the town and its attractions."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0192-b3372c1e155b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SICILY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sicily is mentioned as a region with different cuisine compared to other parts of Italy."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0192-b3372c1e155b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MILAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Milan is mentioned as a city with different cuisine compared to Sicily."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0192-b3372c1e155b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ITALIAN CUISINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Italian cuisine is discussed in terms of regional differences, with emphasis on the uniqueness of each region's culinary traditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0192-b3372c1e155b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VOGHERA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Voghera is a town and 'comune' in the Province of Pavia in the Italian region Lombardy, known for its population, wine production, and historical significance."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0192-b3372c1e155b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PAVIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pavia is a city in the Province of Pavia, Italy, and the second most populated town in the province after Voghera."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0192-b3372c1e155b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VIGEVANO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vigevano is a town in the Province of Pavia, Italy, and the second most populated town in the province after Pavia."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0192-b3372c1e155b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAFFORA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Staffora is a river that flows through Voghera, a tributary of the Po."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0192-b3372c1e155b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Po is a major river in northern Italy, and the Staffora is a tributary of the Po."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0192-b3372c1e155b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IRIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Iria is the ancient name of Voghera, derived from the Latin name 'Forum Iulii Iriensium'."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0192-b3372c1e155b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LONGOBARD TEMPLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Longobard Temple is a historical site in Voghera, known for its significance in the region's history."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0192-b3372c1e155b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IPOGEO CELTICO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ipogeo Celtico is an underground site carved into rock chambers near Voghera, possibly a pre-Roman Celtic site."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0192-b3372c1e155b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLAUSTROPHOBIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Claustrophobia is mentioned as a condition affecting the narrator's experience of visiting the Ipogeo Celtico."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0192-b3372c1e155b</data>
    </node>
    <edge source="&quot;CIVIDALE DEL FRIULI&quot;" target="&quot;NATISONE&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Cividale del Friuli is situated near the river Natisone, which forms a picturesque ravine."</data>
      <data key="d5">"ravine formation, river"</data>
      <data key="d6">ramdocs-0192-b3372c1e155b</data>
    </edge>
  </graph>
</graphml>
